// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  outputs.kdl  —  your screen(s)
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
//  This file is EMPTY on purpose. Screens are set up by kanshi
//  (see home/kanshi.nix), not by niri:
//    • which screens are on (laptop off when a monitor is plugged in)
//    • each screen's size (scale) and refresh rate (Dell: 120 Hz)
//
//  Why not here? When niri re-reads this file it resets every screen
//  to what's written here. If kanshi had turned the laptop screen off,
//  it would pop back on. With one owner (kanshi), they never fight.
//
//  To change a screen: open the Display panel with Super+P.
//  To see your screens' names and modes:   niri msg outputs
